re  we have said it more than once on  visualpolitik the russian economy is  designed so that no business can get out  from under the control of putin and his  elites in that sense russia is totally  efficient however when it comes to  innovation the cielo vicki's are  incapable of generating results so once  again we find that there is a world of  difference between silo vicky  expectation and reality and the truth is  that this is not the first time either  do you remember the russian vaccine  against the coronavirus the famous  sputnik v  [Music]  on paper the vaccine worked that is the  design and the formula were correct i  don't know if you remember but at a time  there was a worldwide debate about the  effectiveness of the russian vaccine  today no one is talking about this  vaccine anymore and it is not even  approved by the who in other words it is  very likely that the russian defense  industry is full of cases like the  sputnik v vaccine we are talking about  combat fighters that on the drawing  board are technological prodigies but  have no ammunition late tank models that  cannot be mass produced because there  are no factories available precision  missiles that are not as accurate as  they appeared to be and so on and so  forth are failed projects for years  putin's entourage has been hiding the  flaws but now that we are seeing the  effectiveness of these weapons on the  battlefield we are seeing that all the  assumptions we had about the russian  economy are true now only one question  remains and i leave it for you to answer  in the comments what about russia's  nuclear weaponry we all know that russia  has the largest nuclear arsenal in the  world putin has even threatened to use  it the question is does it really work  what if many of those warheads are out  of date are those intercontinental  missiles really as effective as the  kremlin claims of course none of us want  to put that to the test but what do you  think is it more russian hype you can  leave me your answers in the comments  below and as always don't forget that  here on visualpolitik we release new  videos every week so subscribe to this  channel hit that little bell icon down  there so you don't miss any of our  updates and if you like this video give  it a like and i'll see you in the next  one  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

